# `val s = "${"$n"}"` - a string inside an interpolation inside a string.
#
# This is the case a stateless hand cannot reach at all: closing correctly
# requires remembering that the `"` at byte 21 opens a *new* string rather
# than closing the one opened at 18. A hand with no memory across the body
# closes the outer string at 21 and reads the rest as code.
#
# Outer [18, 27), inner [21, 25), both read off the source text.
roots 1
mends 0
holds string_literal
holds interpolated_expression
lacks lambda_literal
spans string_literal 18 27
spans string_literal 21 25
